From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:01:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Run the dedicated room unattended

The standalone room waits for input on stdin ("Close with Q+Enter") and
has no signal handling. In a container stdin is closed, so the wait loop
spins on std::cin, and docker stop's SIGTERM kills the process before it
stops announcing the room, saves the ban list or closes the room.

- Replace the stdin loop with a once-a-second check of the room state and
  a flag set by SIGINT and SIGTERM. Stopping the process now runs the
  normal shutdown path: announce cleanup, ban list save, room Destroy().
- --username takes a required argument. With optional_argument,
  "--username name" left optarg null and crashed when it was read.

Tests: the image's startup/shutdown check and tests/test_room_protocol.py
stop the room with SIGTERM and require a clean exit, not a kill.
---
 src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp | 26 +++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

